From eff5233235e14a0d4c93489efddd004e1fadd204 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EX20v porter <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:36:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] econet-eth: use the EX20v port's driver with PPE hardware
 offload

Replace the econet-eth package with the one from the TP-Link EX20v (v1)
OpenWrt port (github.com/ozgunokan/openwrt-tplink-ex20v): econet_eth
1db74f8 plus its patch set, which adds PPE/FOE hardware flow offload,
TX/NAPI fixes and the EX20v internal-GSW WAN/LAN VLAN split.

EX20v v2 uses the same GSW port mapping as v1, so it switches to that
setup: the DSA switch is disabled, LAN is eth0.1, WAN is eth0.35 (PPPoE,
Turk Telekom) or eth0.2 (untagged). The front panel port LEDs are handed
to the GPHY LED function.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
