+From: OpenAI Codex <codex@local>
+Subject: econet-eth: include TRGMII resync in delayed MT7530 reapply
+
+Reboot testing on Archer C5v still showed occasional wired Ethernet loss after
+the initial TRGMII resync. The delayed work previously only re-applied the
+external MT7530 VLAN/port table, which does not recover a dead TRGMII data path
+when registers already read back correctly.
+
+Run the TRGMII pad resync before each delayed VLAN split reapply and extend the
+retry window to 2s, 10s, 30s, 60s and 120s. Both operations are idempotent for
+the C5v VLAN-split path and keep the existing topology unchanged.
