++			 * entry often enough to ask us to bind it. Only act here:
++			 * the UNBIND entry is guaranteed present (it was just hit)
++			 * so the table scan finds it first try, and this fires
++			 * roughly once per hot flow instead of on every miss -
++			 * the per-packet scan was saturating the CPU. Plain
++			 * UN_HIT/HIT_UNBIND (0x0d/0x0e) are left on the slow path. */
