diff --git a/package/kernel/econet-eth/patches/153-ppe-only-gdm-egress.patch b/package/kernel/econet-eth/patches/153-ppe-only-gdm-egress.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..d341a26727
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/econet-eth/patches/153-ppe-only-gdm-egress.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+From: Emre Yavuzalp <emreyavuzalp@gmail.com>
+Subject: econet-eth: only offload flows whose egress is the GDM netdev
+
+Every accepted flow is bound with PSE egress GDM1 (patch 130), but the
+FLOW_ACTION_REDIRECT target device was never checked ("3b" was never
+finished). Flows towards a Wi-Fi client also reach us - through the
+indirect flow block on phy0-ap0/phy1-ap0 or with the redirect pointing
+at the other direction's ingress when the forward path does not resolve
+(XMIT_NEIGH) - and carry a perfectly valid L2 rewrite (dst = station
+MAC), so they bound too. The hardware then switched those packets out
+the wired MT7530 ports where the station's MAC never lives: download to
+any Wi-Fi client black-holed as soon as the flow bound, which is why
+speed tests over Wi-Fi never started while wired stayed at line rate.
+
+Record GDM1's netdev on the PPE at probe and reject any flow whose
+redirect target is a different device; those flows now stay on the
+(software) flowtable path. Wired flows still resolve to the GDM netdev
+and keep full hardware offload.
+--- a/econet_ppe.h	2026-07-03 09:08:55.338745936 +0300
